What Is an M3U IPTV Playlist?

An .m3u or .m3u8 file is a text playlist containing TV channel or video stream links.

Example:

#EXTM3U

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="news" group-title="News",CNN
https://example.com/live/cnn.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="sports" group-title="Sports",ESPN
https://example.com/live/espn.m3u8
1. Create Your Own IPTV M3U Playlist

You can make one manually.

Step 1 — Open Notepad

Use:

Notepad
VS Code
Sublime Text
Step 2 — Add Playlist Code

Example:

#EXTM3U

#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Movies",Movie Channel
https://test-streams.mux.dev/x36xhzz/x36xhzz.m3u8

#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Sports TV
https://demo.unified-streaming.com/k8s/features/stable/video/tears-of-steel/tears-of-steel.ism/.m3u8
Step 3 — Save File

Save as:

myiptv.m3u

Encoding:

UTF-8
